 Nursery Data Integated Report
Data #1: Access Logs- 
The system is for the nursery logging system.
Information was recorded to identify timestamps, person identification, type of person, nurses, parents, or patients.
Format was CSV.

Data #2: Newborn vital signs- 
The system is for the monitoring system. 
Information was recorded for heart rates, breathing rates, temperatures,and newborn condition.
Format was XML.

Data #3 Room Sensors- 
The system is for room monitoring.
Information was recorded to indentify room numbers, time stamps, room temperatures, door status, and humidity.
Format was JSON.

timestamp: The data and time associated with a record. 

record_type: Identifies the type of record, such as access_log, newborn_vitals, or room_sensor.

source_file: Identifies the original file from which the record came.

room: Stores the room identifier when available.

person_id and person_type: Describe the person listed in an access-log record.

patient_id: Identifies the newborn associated with a vital-sign record.

heart_rate_bpm, breathing_rate_per_min, and temperature_f: Store newborn measurements when available.

room_temperature_f, door_status, and humidity: Store environmental information when available.

has_medical_condition and medical_condition: Provide fields for condition information when it is present in the integrated data.
